      "content": "Strict gun control advocates still have a variety of legal arguments to make, even concerning the Bruen ruling. The arguments can include the applicability of state and local controls that are consistent with historical precedent, the separate sovereign nature of state governments versus federal government, the ongoing public safety concerns, and focusing on bans for specific personages, like felons and the mentally ill, which have a longer tradition of legal permissibility. Thus, while Bruen certainly affects the landscape, it doesn't render all forms of gun control unconstitutional.",
